Z||000000||Ferrari355||02-22-2000||06:15 PM||||Hello everyone, we jut got back from the bank and the loan was approved. I'm so glad. My parents were going to buy it ans keep it at my dads friends house until my birthday which is september 17 (was born in 85). I didn't even know about it either. I think that will be awesome. WE might go pick it up tomorrow becasue my dad will get off one of his jobs at around 1:30 central and then we will run to the bank and then maybe we will drive to Tulsa, OK to pick it up since i don't have school tomorrow becasue a lady who worked at the school died and her funeral is tomorrow. But we will most likely buy it. If not i will be so pissed off. But i think we are going to anyway. My dad had to talk my mom into buying it. she said he was bugging her about it for a month or so. But i have a few questions. One the first day you guys bought your fiero. What did you do? Did you take pics of it right when you got it? I'm going too. And what do yuo suggest i do when i first get it besides stare at it and beg mom to let me drive it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But i guess i'll take alot of pics and then post them. Well i better go, let me know what you think. BYe<BR>Alex...||||reg||10
Z||000001||stimpy||02-22-2000||07:13 PM||||Congratulations!! <BR>One of the first things I did was take it to a coin op carwash that had an engine degreaser setting and cleaned the gunk off.  It always amazes me when people pop the deck on their Fiero to show a filthy engine. The V6, for all its shortcomings, is a beautiful engine. Also, a dirty engne is a hotter engine. Make sure you keep any spray away from the alternator and the distributor, bu hose the gunk away!<BR>Also, I drove the hell out of my Fiero when I first got it. Still do every chance I get!  Have fun with it Alex!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-22-2000||08:05 PM||||Congrats.!!!! Alex the best thing to do the first night is sleep in it, maybe 2-3 nights, get to know it real good, then take a few parts off and take them with you, to school, to work, to the mall, show them a good time, the shift knob, ya the knob, take it off put it in your pocket  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ok,ok, do what you want<P>Good luck!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||Ferrari355||02-22-2000||08:31 PM||||HEHE, that was funny. I don't think i'll be taking anything apart. I will baby the car. Well i got to go, I'll be online LATER tonight cause my dad was mad when he tried to call and i was online. THANKS EVERYONE. Bye<BR>Alex....||||reg||10
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-22-2000||08:37 PM||||You can solve the phone problem easily.  Just do what I did.  Get a 2nd phone line dedicated to the computer.  Now Monkeygirl can talk on the phone while I "talk" on the computer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||02-22-2000||09:38 PM||||Here is the very 1st picture I took of my car.  It was parked in front of my brother's house.  This was even before my wife knew I had it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar_1.jpg"> <P>P.S.<BR>I bought a call waiting modem. It didn't work like i wanted it to. I had to disconnect from the internet to answer the phone.  I then downloaded a free program that is an internet answering machine.  You have to subscribe to busy call forwarding from your phone company for it to work.  Here is the link to it.  Check it out. <A HREF="http://www.commission-junction.com/track/track.dll?AID=44071&PID=131578&URL=http%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Ecallwave%2Ecom" TARGET=_blank>http://www.commission-junction.com/track/track.dll?AID=44071&PID=131578&URL=http%3A%2F%2Fwww%2Ecallwave%2Ecom</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||02-22-2000||10:04 PM||||Don't (and I repeat) DO NOT wash a hot engine, you might crack something expensive on the motor. Then you'll cry. High pressure isn't the best under the hood anyway. Use an engine degreaser and a regular garden hose at home with a COLD engine if you must clean the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||02-22-2000||10:39 PM||||I agree with DAD, sleep in it when ever you can!  Heck, mine has been in my garage (broken) since last June, and I would go out and climb in it and just sit and relax... and dream!  Of course, now that it's on jack stands, I don't do that any more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As for a part to carry around, I would suggest the fuel pump fuse... so your parents can't take the car without you!  At least, they can't go very far if they try  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
