Z||000013||stimpy||02-23-2000||07:50 AM||||Ok, my turn to caution you on something.... Don't screw around with your radiator!!!!! Sure, you may want to have your system flushed, in that case take it to a shop. It's worth it to have someone else liable if it gets screwed up.  I made the mistake of putting thoe dress-up "steel braided" hose covers on my dads car. I topped off the system when I was done and within a week the radiator had a fatal crack. <BR>Lesson bought- the Fiero has a pressrized coolant system. Amatuers beware!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ferrari355||02-23-2000||12:32 PM||||Thanks everyone for your info. I will imagine once we get it I will definatly clean it up inside and out all the time. The sad thing is that my dad is going to drive it to work, because it is going to be his work car. He bought it to keep the miles off the Trans Am  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I will still clean it every chance i get. Anyway, i don't think we are going to get it today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> but we are going to get it this Saturday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> I wanted it today, I CAN'T WAIT MUCH LONGER!!!<BR>But, i guess i'll have to. Maybe i can talk dad into staying home today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I hope so. Anyway, i better go... Thanks for your info. I'll be back later. Bye,<BR>Alex....||||reg||10
